<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Seartec half yr shr rises, div steady.</title>
<headline>Seartec half yr shr rises, div steady.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     10.7     vs  10.5</p>
<p>    Interim div (cts)	2.5     vs   2.5</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   10.2     vs   9.9</p>
<p>    After tax		  6.7     vs   6.3</p>
<p>    Interest paid	    0.07    vs   0.4</p>
<p>    Turnover		 114.58    vs 118.38</p>
<p>Div payable: April 4</p>
<p>On register: March 20</p>
<p>Full name: Seartec Ltd (trading as Sharp Electronics SA)</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said it had been affected by consumers' limited discretionary income. Its distribution agreement with Sharp Electronics of Japan would be renewed by November 1997 for another five years, ensuring that the group stayed at the forefront of latest technology.</p>
<p>It said it was well-positioned to take advantage of the improved rand/dollar exchange rate and that exciting technological developments in the video and television industries could ensure growth in future.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
